<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marko's Monastery</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1345–1377</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Markov Manastir</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marko's Monastery is a Serbian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> monastery of Saint Demetrius in the village of Markova Sušica near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skopje">Skopje</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a>. Its church was begun in 1345 by Vukašin and completed around 1376–77 by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-marko">Prince Marko</a>, whose portraits appear among its frescoes. It is one of the best-preserved monuments of 14th-century Byzantine-style painting in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/markos-monastery.jpg" alt="Marko's Monastery" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dimitar Georgievski from Skopje, Macedonia · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marko-Monastery-church.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
